    <briefdescription>
<para>Armijo line search. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Let <formula id="3">$ \alpha $</formula> and <formula id="220">$ \beta $</formula> be 2 scalars in <formula id="221">$ [0,1] $</formula>. Let <formula id="134">$ x $</formula> be the current value of the unknown, <formula id="222">$ d $</formula> the search direction and <formula id="147">$ t $</formula> the step. Let <formula id="37">$ f $</formula> be the function to minimize. The line search stops when <formula id="147">$ t $</formula> verifies <formula id="223">\[ f(x + t \cdot d) - f(x) \leq -\alpha t f&apos;(x+t \cdot d) \]</formula> and <formula id="224">\[ f(x+\frac{t}{\beta} \cdot d) - f(x) &gt; -\frac{\alpha}{\beta} t f&apos;(x+t \cdot d) \]</formula> <verbatim>  (see Polak, Algorithms and consistent approximations, Optimization,
  volume 124 of Applied Mathematical Sciences, Springer-Verlag, NY,
  1997)</verbatim> </para>    </detaileddescription>
    <location file="/math/optimization/armijo.hpp" line="48" bodyfile="/math/optimization/armijo.hpp" bodystart="48" bodyend="63"/>
